# Command (from the repo root, zig 0.14.1 x86_64-linux, the pinned one in tools/.toolchain):
#   make -C platforms/anyka-ak3918 repro        (AKAM_REPRO=1, SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH=0, -ffile-prefix-map, -g0, zig objcopy --strip-all)
# Check: tools/ci/repro_check.sh. A different zig changes the hash: update this file in the same commit as the pin.
# 2026-11-23, feat/1080p-parity-b: new hash a96996a5... (was e4552748...). Intentional behaviour change: new module image_orient.c (rows image.flip, image.mirror, image.ceiling; ISP flip call 0x40044979 sent only when a flip or mirror is saved or set; nothing is sent by default, no file is read beyond one fopen of /etc/config/akam/orient at start). Default behaviour unchanged. Proof: tests/ak1080_settings_test.sh and ak1080_api_http_test.sh (orientation rows against a fake ISP call, nothing sent while off).
# 2026-11-23, feat/1080p-parity-b (second step): new hash 67c8f2a4... (was a96996a5...). Intentional: the flip / mirror call is replayed after each day/night ISP reload (night.c, nothing sent while both are off), two Home Assistant switch entities (image_flip, image_mirror) in the MQTT table and their read through control_get_value. Defaults unchanged. Proof: tests/ak1080_settings_test.sh (replay cases), tests/mqtt_ha_test.sh (entities and commands).
# 2026-11-23, merge of fix/2k-parity-a (mic opt-in, ST_SECRET_WO) and feat/1080p-parity-b (flip/mirror): combined hash, both intentional changes above.
# 2026-11-23, feat/api-only-8091-closed: new hash e44785e7... (was f897c806...). Behaviour change: the text port 8091 binds 127.0.0.1 unless the saved opt-in /etc/config/akam/control_lan is on (control_lan_get at start, control_lan_set written only on a change); the registry gets img.wb, audio.out_volume/out_enable/talk_enable/mic_enable, control.lan and the state rows net.ssid, net.wifi_rate, led.state, audio.out_state/underruns/drops (through the existing control_get_value / control_apply_setting, so one writer per value as before), the action audio.beep, and MAX_ROWS 60 -> 80. The video, audio and RTSP paths are untouched.
# 2026-11-23, feat/api-only-8091-closed (second change): new hash 3a47566a... (was e44785e7...). Behaviour change: a PATCH reply says "saved":false for a key whose setter applied the value but could not write its file (streg_note_unsaved in src/core/settings_reg.c, called by the 1080p legacy and LED-pattern setters); nothing else changes. The shared registry code is also in the 2K binary: its golden (tests/golden/rot2k_app.golden) was regenerated for the same reason, the 2K never calls it.
# 2026-11-23, fix/2k-latency: new hash c49b441b... (was f897c806...). Intentional behaviour change on the 1080p, shared TCP video pacing: SO_SNDBUF 256 KiB -> 64 KiB (TX_PACE_SNDBUF), a latency bound in tx_pace (a backlog standing above the idle level for 300 ms plus the keyframe's time at the nominal rate drops the client to the next keyframe), and a per-client frame-age line in the log (lat_stat.h, every 10 s). Proof: tests/tx_pace_test.sh (old assertions unchanged, new ones for the bound), tests/pace_compose_test.sh, tests/rot2k_latency_test.sh. NOT flashed on a 1080p.
# 2026-11-23, merge of feat/api-only-8091-closed and fix/2k-latency: combined hash, both intentional changes above.
# 2026-11-23, reorg/step7-akamd: new hash c2a2a603... (was c05b14b6...). Behaviour identical: the program is named akamd on every camera, so the strings that named it changed (the klog usage line, the img.venc_rc hint, the audio crash-guard note, the SDP session name s=akamd); the log prefix [ak_rtsp] is kept on purpose. Proof: the dev tree at the same sources reproduces c05b14b6... and the only differences in `strings` are those four texts (.text moves with the string addresses), tests/rtsp_sdp tests and the host suite pass.
