# 2026-11-23, fix/2k-parity-a: new hash 121e145a... (was e4552748...). Behaviour change: the 1080p microphone is off by default (audio.mic_enable default 0, opt-in, same as the 2K; a saved explicit value is kept). Also shared-code change in settings_reg (ST_SECRET_WO write-only rows and a PATCH reply that never echoes a secret row; the 1080p table has no secret row, so nothing else changes). Proof: tests/native/audio_out_test.c (new default, save/reload of an explicit value), tests/ak1080_settings_test.sh, tests/ak1080_api_http_test.sh.
# 2026-11-23, feat/2k-audio-picture: new hash d8fb281b... (was e4552748...). Behaviour identical on the 1080p; only code placement and one start-up call changed: the speaker engine (audio_out.c) and the talk session (talk.c) moved unchanged from platforms/anyka-ak3918 to src/features/audio (shared with the 2K), the playback ioctl numbers to src/hal/akpcm.h (same values), and its singleton no longer names the device or the conf dir: main() now calls audio_out_setup("/dev/pcmC0D0p", "/etc/config/akam", 1), the values the singleton hard-coded before (speaker enabled by default as before). Proof: tests/audio_out_test.sh and tests/talk_test.sh (same assertions, only the paths of the sources), rtsp_backchannel_test.sh, control_test.sh, onvif_media_test.sh unchanged. NOT validated on a 1080p camera with this build: the 1080p hardware results come from earlier builds (docs/testing-status.md).
